WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.953
How does AI write a sentence? A language model predicts the next piece of text, called a token.

00:00:06.953 --> 00:00:13.906
A token might be a whole word, a word part, or punctuation. The text so far provides context.

00:00:13.906 --> 00:00:21.246
After the cat sat on the, mat might be likely. Moon is possible, but less likely. These example probabilities

00:00:21.246 --> 00:00:22.405
are made up.

00:00:22.405 --> 00:00:29.744
The system chooses a token, adds it to the sentence, and predicts again. Repeating this can produce a whole

00:00:29.744 --> 00:00:30.130
paragraph.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:36.697
A setting called temperature changes how varied the choices are. More variety does not mean more truth.

00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:43.651
A fluent answer can still be wrong. Treat important answers as a starting point, and check the evidence.
